1
00:00:09,180 --> 00:00:11,795
Dependent arising, without arising.

2
00:00:11,875 --> 00:00:13,710
It sounds like a contradiction.

3
00:00:13,790 --> 00:00:16,514
Nāgārjuna opens his whole work with it.

4
00:00:17,320 --> 00:00:19,948
I am John Tan, known as Thusness.

5
00:00:20,028 --> 00:00:23,906
These are my own notes, from my
own practice and contemplation.

6
00:00:24,716 --> 00:00:28,716
Section 5 stayed with the twelve
links as the tradition teaches them.

7
00:00:28,796 --> 00:00:32,344
A chain of conditions, from
ignorance to ageing and death,

8
00:00:32,424 --> 00:00:34,522
with no one in it who goes round.

9
00:00:35,328 --> 00:00:37,766
Behind that reading stood the Abhidharma.

10
00:00:37,846 --> 00:00:40,809
It took the person apart
into momentary factors,

11
00:00:40,889 --> 00:00:42,644
and found no self among them.

12
00:00:42,724 --> 00:00:46,828
But it kept the factors themselves
as real, each with its own nature.

13
00:00:46,908 --> 00:00:50,918
And it read dependent arising as the law
by which one real factor produces the

14
00:00:50,998 --> 00:00:52,198
next.

15
00:00:52,684 --> 00:00:55,937
This section reads the same
teaching with Nāgārjuna.

16
00:00:56,017 --> 00:00:57,731
He keeps the twelve links.

17
00:00:57,811 --> 00:01:01,562
But he reads the sentence beneath them
in a way that changes what the links,

18
00:01:01,642 --> 00:01:03,428
and the pieces, are.

19
00:01:04,232 --> 00:01:05,991
When this is, that is.

20
00:01:06,071 --> 00:01:08,857
From the arising of this, that arises.

21
00:01:08,937 --> 00:01:11,126
When this is not, that is not.

22
00:01:11,206 --> 00:01:13,916
From the ceasing of this, that ceases.

23
00:01:14,724 --> 00:01:18,534
The sentence holds two kinds
of line. Some speak of being.

24
00:01:18,614 --> 00:01:20,368
When this is, that is.

25
00:01:20,448 --> 00:01:23,127
Two things found together,
and missing together.

26
00:01:23,207 --> 00:01:24,879
Others speak of arising.

27
00:01:24,959 --> 00:01:27,746
From the arising of this, that arises.

28
00:01:27,826 --> 00:01:30,020
These sound like a sequence in time.

29
00:01:30,832 --> 00:01:35,009
As I see it, the difference between
the two readings begins right here.

30
00:01:35,089 --> 00:01:38,256
Is when this is, that
is, heard as a handover,

31
00:01:38,336 --> 00:01:40,186
something passing from this to that?

32
00:01:40,266 --> 00:01:43,338
Or as a pattern, two
things found only together?

33
00:01:43,418 --> 00:01:45,892
The traditional reading hears a handover.

34
00:01:45,972 --> 00:01:48,016
Nāgārjuna hears a pattern.

35
00:01:48,812 --> 00:01:50,937
He opens his Middle Way with a bow.

36
00:01:51,017 --> 00:01:53,383
Without ceasing, without arising.

37
00:01:53,463 --> 00:01:56,114
Without annihilation, without permanence.

38
00:01:56,194 --> 00:01:58,261
Not one thing and not many.

39
00:01:58,341 --> 00:02:00,503
Without coming and without going.

40
00:02:00,583 --> 00:02:03,288
So the awakened one
taught dependent arising,

41
00:02:03,368 --> 00:02:06,037
the quieting of elaborations, peace.

42
00:02:06,840 --> 00:02:09,713
How can dependent arising
be without arising?

43
00:02:10,516 --> 00:02:13,063
The answer is the key
to the whole difference.

44
00:02:13,143 --> 00:02:16,079
If a sprout could be found
arising from its seed,

45
00:02:16,159 --> 00:02:18,103
it would have an arising of its own.

46
00:02:18,183 --> 00:02:20,196
And then it would not need to depend.

47
00:02:20,276 --> 00:02:24,847
That it depends is exactly why no
arising is found, when it is sought.

48
00:02:25,640 --> 00:02:29,813
On the traditional reading, dependent
arising is a law about how real things

49
00:02:29,893 --> 00:02:30,836
arise.

50
00:02:30,916 --> 00:02:35,673
On Nāgārjuna's reading, dependent arising
is why nothing is found to arise in that

51
00:02:35,753 --> 00:02:36,953
way at all.

52
00:02:37,524 --> 00:02:43,141
He puts it in one line. Not from
itself. Not from another. Not from both.

53
00:02:43,221 --> 00:02:44,772
And not without a cause.

54
00:02:44,852 --> 00:02:48,322
No thing, anywhere, is
ever found to have arisen.

55
00:02:49,120 --> 00:02:52,197
These are the only ways
a real thing could arise.

56
00:02:52,277 --> 00:02:54,778
From itself, and it was already there.

57
00:02:54,858 --> 00:02:59,398
From another, and something must cross
the gap between two complete things.

58
00:02:59,478 --> 00:03:01,218
Nothing is found crossing.

59
00:03:01,298 --> 00:03:04,225
Without a cause, and the
world would not work.

60
00:03:05,036 --> 00:03:08,072
Notice what is refused. Not causes.

61
00:03:08,152 --> 00:03:09,784
Not the order of the world.

62
00:03:09,864 --> 00:03:11,781
What is refused is production.

63
00:03:11,861 --> 00:03:16,419
A real thing, standing on its own,
bringing about another real thing.

64
00:03:17,232 --> 00:03:20,322
So what is a condition,
if it does not produce?

65
00:03:21,124 --> 00:03:24,785
These are conditions, because in
dependence on them that arises.

66
00:03:24,865 --> 00:03:29,830
So it is said. But until that has
arisen, why are these not non-conditions?

67
00:03:30,632 --> 00:03:35,502
A seed is not a cause sitting there with a
power inside it, waiting to hand it over.

68
00:03:35,582 --> 00:03:38,138
It is called a cause
because there is a sprout.

69
00:03:38,218 --> 00:03:41,127
Being a condition is named
from the effect's side,

70
00:03:41,207 --> 00:03:42,757
together with the effect.

71
00:03:42,837 --> 00:03:45,289
As long and short are named together.

72
00:03:46,092 --> 00:03:48,027
Fire and fuel are the same.

73
00:03:48,107 --> 00:03:53,018
There is no fuel apart from what burns,
and no fire apart from what it burns.

74
00:03:53,824 --> 00:03:57,145
One caution here, because
this is easily misheard.

75
00:03:57,225 --> 00:04:00,379
Named together does not mean
happening at the same time.

76
00:04:00,459 --> 00:04:02,824
The seed still comes before the sprout.

77
00:04:02,904 --> 00:04:05,981
What is mutual is the
defining, not the timing.

78
00:04:06,788 --> 00:04:09,960
It helps to separate three
things the word cause can mean.

79
00:04:10,040 --> 00:04:11,780
Production is refused.

80
00:04:11,860 --> 00:04:15,394
A cause that exists on its
own, and delivers an effect,

81
00:04:15,474 --> 00:04:18,859
as goods come out of a
factory. Alignment is kept.

82
00:04:18,939 --> 00:04:21,903
Factors come together,
and a result appears.

83
00:04:21,983 --> 00:04:23,859
And designation is kept.

84
00:04:23,939 --> 00:04:26,454
Cause is the part that
attention picks out,

85
00:04:26,534 --> 00:04:28,755
when it lays a process out in order.

86
00:04:29,568 --> 00:04:33,840
A bell is struck. Bronze,
the strike, the air, the ear.

87
00:04:33,920 --> 00:04:37,155
The ringing is not made by
these, and then sent out.

88
00:04:37,235 --> 00:04:40,566
The ringing is their
meeting, vivid and complete.

89
00:04:40,646 --> 00:04:44,302
Change one condition, a
cracked bell, a gust of wind,

90
00:04:44,382 --> 00:04:46,530
and it is not the same sound altered.

91
00:04:46,610 --> 00:04:48,872
It is a different sound altogether.

92
00:04:49,684 --> 00:04:51,551
Now return to the sentence.

93
00:04:51,631 --> 00:04:53,471
When this is, that is.

94
00:04:54,272 --> 00:04:57,376
On the traditional reading,
it describes a handover.

95
00:04:57,456 --> 00:05:01,099
On Nāgārjuna's reading, it
describes a pattern holding.

96
00:05:01,179 --> 00:05:05,107
Leave out the yeast, and the
loaf is flat, in every kitchen.

97
00:05:05,187 --> 00:05:07,702
That reliability needs no handover.

98
00:05:07,782 --> 00:05:10,532
Nothing passes from the
yeast into the loaf.

99
00:05:11,340 --> 00:05:14,897
And the sentence never said
production. It said when.

100
00:05:15,712 --> 00:05:19,712
This is not a weaker dependent
arising. It is a stronger one.

101
00:05:19,792 --> 00:05:23,299
A seed with its own nature
could not give rise to anything.

102
00:05:23,379 --> 00:05:27,416
It could not change, so it
could not sprout. Things work.

103
00:05:27,496 --> 00:05:29,540
And what works is found empty.

104
00:05:30,356 --> 00:05:34,778
From here Nāgārjuna draws the line
that joins everything in this series.

105
00:05:34,858 --> 00:05:37,672
Dependent arising is
what we call emptiness.

106
00:05:37,752 --> 00:05:40,063
That is a designation in dependence.

107
00:05:40,143 --> 00:05:42,173
And that itself is the middle way.

108
00:05:42,984 --> 00:05:46,831
On the traditional reading, dependent
arising and emptiness could be two

109
00:05:46,911 --> 00:05:51,061
teachings. On Nāgārjuna's
reading, they are one fact.

110
00:05:51,141 --> 00:05:55,082
That a thing depends is exactly
why it has no nature of its own.

111
00:05:55,162 --> 00:05:59,326
And that it has no nature of its
own is exactly why it can depend.

112
00:06:00,124 --> 00:06:03,744
So the Abhidharma's work is
carried one step further.

113
00:06:03,824 --> 00:06:05,510
It found the person empty.

114
00:06:05,590 --> 00:06:09,885
Nāgārjuna finds the pieces empty
too. Not because they are nothing.

115
00:06:09,965 --> 00:06:12,689
Because each is what it
is only with the others.

116
00:06:13,496 --> 00:06:15,961
He does not present
this as a new teaching.

117
00:06:16,041 --> 00:06:18,651
He presents it as what the
Buddha meant all along.

118
00:06:18,731 --> 00:06:21,668
He singles out one discourse, to Kaccāna.

119
00:06:21,748 --> 00:06:25,526
There the Buddha says the world
mostly leans on two ideas.

120
00:06:25,606 --> 00:06:27,483
It is, and it is not.

121
00:06:27,563 --> 00:06:31,985
Avoiding both, he teaches by
the middle. The twelve links.

122
00:06:32,796 --> 00:06:35,818
A chain of real things would
sit on the side of it is.

123
00:06:35,898 --> 00:06:40,089
The Buddha set both sides aside,
and taught the chain as the middle.

124
00:06:40,888 --> 00:06:45,907
So, as I read it, the difference is
not between Nāgārjuna and the Buddha.

125
00:06:45,987 --> 00:06:49,798
It is between Nāgārjuna and
one way of reading the Buddha.

126
00:06:50,612 --> 00:06:52,819
Return to the harsh word at work.

127
00:06:52,899 --> 00:06:57,316
On the first reading, the word is a
real thing that produced a real feeling,

128
00:06:57,396 --> 00:06:59,246
which produced a real craving.

129
00:06:59,326 --> 00:07:01,967
Then the task is to manage the dominoes.

130
00:07:02,784 --> 00:07:05,897
On the second reading,
the word, the hearing,

131
00:07:05,977 --> 00:07:09,624
the feeling and the one who is
hurt are found only together.

132
00:07:09,704 --> 00:07:13,401
The hurt is vivid, and it
follows its conditions exactly.

133
00:07:13,481 --> 00:07:16,268
But nothing in it was
handed over from outside.

134
00:07:16,348 --> 00:07:18,406
And nothing in it stands on its own.

135
00:07:19,204 --> 00:07:23,259
This is Section 6, Part 1 of
the Dependent Arising series.

136
00:07:24,056 --> 00:07:27,133
When this is, that is. Not a handover.

137
00:07:27,213 --> 00:07:29,107
A pattern, holding.

